record(s,t,r,d,inv,"The sheet discusses compact quotient tori and then gives Corollaire 1 about V_K/V_K0 and the unit subgroup. The first attempt is cancelled, including an unfinished equality. The live proof passes to the real base and displays the quotient by G_m as a product of circles. It concludes with the implication (iv)⇒(i). Written slips are retained: the proof switches from K_0 to L_0; K_R ≃ C^{*r} contains a star; the degree is [K_0:K]=r; the last norm is N_{L/K}, while the preceding page wrote N_{K/L} for the map from K to L. Local dimension check 142.N1: the displayed K_0 tensor R ≃ R^r gives dim_Q K_0=r, since a Q-basis tensors to an R-basis. This identifies Q as the degree base used by that calculation, while the ink plainly has K. The index order and star were retained, not silently repaired. Archive number 141 appears at the foot.",doubts=doubts,notation=[['Cancelled unfinished equality','L_0R = followed by blank paper','142','No illegible-content token is added for the blank.'],['Author’s spelling','wailien on this leaf','142','Closed a after w; other leaves are read independently.']],hand=['A circle and arrow relocate compacts to after quotients; underlining survives the relocation. C omitted the underline and H retained the earlier order.','Inserted T and main-line V are distinct on this page: the flat crossbar of T_L0 in the interline is visible. Both witnesses read V there.','Short en/in and a openings can be nearly flat: the final noun remains marked instead of being settled from grammar.'],abbreviations=[['gr.','groupe'],['gr','groupe'],['respectivmt','respectivement'],['1ère','première']],events=[['142.N1','targeted proof check','Tensoring a Q-basis to R preserves the finite dimension. The displayed R^r therefore identifies dim_Q K_0 as r; the written [K_0:K] was retained.']])
